###############################################################################
# Project‑specific exclusions / re‑includes
###############################################################################

# Obsolete
memory/**
instruments/**
knowledge/custom/**

# Logs, tmp, usr
logs/*
tmp/*
usr/*

# Pinned developer tooling. Gitignored already, but that does not reach the
# Docker build context -- 125 MB of local binaries were shipping in every image.
deploy/dev/.bin/

# Licensed vendor lab images (Cisco, F5, ...) for a local test lab.
# Gitignored already, and the same lesson again: on 2026-10-11 three of them,
# 3 GB, went into the application image and made a 10 GB ISO.
image/
.pytest_cache/


# Keep .gitkeep markers anywhere
!**/.gitkeep


###############################################################################
# Environment / tooling
###############################################################################
.conda/
.cursor/
# Agent worktrees live under .claude/worktrees/: whole copies of this and other repositories, which a local build
# put into the image (UAT, 2026-10-19).
.claude/
.venv/
.git/
# The Playwright MCP's screenshots, logs and whatever a test hands the
# browser to upload -- a 3 GB update bundle, once.
.playwright-mcp/


###############################################################################
# Tests (root‑level only)
###############################################################################
/*.test.py


###############################################################################
# Never delivered to a customer
#
# The image goes to companies who buy this product. None of the following
# is a credential, and none of it lets anyone forge a licence -- the
# signing key never leaves the licence server. But it is all internal
# material that benefits the recipient not at all.
#
# tests/test_delivery_hygiene.py asserts these stay out of a built image.
###############################################################################
# Decision records, roadmaps, and the licensing strategy itself.
docs/internal/
# The sales presentation: two megabytes of screenshots nobody needs inside a customer's container.
docs/presentation/

# Test names and fixtures describe internal behaviour and security
# assumptions; nothing at runtime imports from here.
tests/

# The release signing tool. Its own docstring says "never shipped" --
# this is what makes that true.
scripts/sign_release.py

# Internal engineering process.
CONTRIBUTING.md

# The same kind of material in other folders. graphify-out/ is a generated
# graph of the whole repository, 41 MB, and it quotes docs/internal/ -- the
# licensing plan included -- so excluding docs/internal/ alone did not keep
# that text out. The rest is notes, plans and tool configuration.
graphify-out/
handoff/
obsidion-note/
docs/plans/
.github/
.hermes/
.vscode/

# The development stack's own secrets. docker/run/.env and the runner's SSH
# key pair are gitignored, so they exist only on the machine that builds the
# image -- which is the one place they could get into it from. They did:
# `*.env` at the bottom of this file matched the root only.
docker/run/runner_key
docker/run/runner_key.pub
**/*.pem

# A UAT build's licence trust (ADR 0085). build_local.sh reads REZZTOR_UAT_TRUST
# (uat-trust.json in its example) and passes it as a build argument, and the image
# build writes licence_trust.json itself. A copy lying in the working folder must
# never enter the context: a non-UAT image would carry a dummy root beside it.
**/uat-trust.json
**/licence_trust.json

# The local DEV setup (dev/run.sh): its settings, keys and data, and the stamp it
# writes into the working tree so that a host run trusts the licence server's DEV
# root. An image build writes its own build_info.json; this one must not be there
# for it to find.
dev/
build_info.json

# The public marketing website at rezztor.com lives in its own repository now
# (a separate website repository), so there is normally no site/ here to
# exclude. The entry stays because working on both at once usually means a
# checkout or a symlink at this path, and a node_modules arriving in the build
# context is worth hundreds of megabytes on a runner whose disk is already
# the binding constraint.
site/

###############################################################################
# Engineering material: what explains the code, tests it or builds it
#
# The owner's rule (2026-10-12): a customer gets what the machine runs and
# nothing that documents how it is made. 210 file-level notes, 130 AGENTS.md
# contracts, CLAUDE.md, the developer guides, every plugin's tests and the
# scripts that build the ISO were all in the delivered image until then.
#
# Nothing at run time reads any of it. The AGENTS.md the product does read
# is a customer's own, in a project under usr/. Skills are found by SKILL.md.
# A plugin with no README.md shows no "Read me" on the Plugins screen.
#
# What the build needs but the machine does not (docker/, the frontend
# sources, requirements.txt) cannot be listed here; the Dockerfile's assemble
# step removes it. scripts/build_offline_bundle.sh looks inside the built
# images and stops when any of this is back.
###############################################################################
**/*.dox.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/README.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/
**/tests/
**/conftest.py
testsupport.py
pytest.ini
requirements.dev.txt
mise.toml
jsconfig.json
deploy/
# Four of its files do go into the image: they also live on the appliance's own
# disk, and an update package takes the new ones from the image it is made of
# (HOST in scripts/sign_release.py). So do the public release keys, so that an
# update can add one (NEW_KEY there); support/ stays out, no update touches it.
!deploy/customer/docker-compose.yml
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-update
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-setup
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-network
# The guard and the units an update package may carry (ADR 0092; scripts/sign_release.py, HOST).
!deploy/customer/rezztor-guard
!deploy/customer/rezztor-guard.service
!deploy/customer/rezztor-guard-runner.service
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-firewall.service
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-load-images.service
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-setup.service
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-update.service
!deploy/iso/host/rezztor-update.path
!deploy/iso/keys/*.pub
scripts/
**/Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Read by the agent at run time, and still a description of how the product
# is built inside. The owner's decision of 2026-10-12: the six skills for
# developing the framework and its plugins stay here, and so does the note
# that lists the main files. "Create an agent profile", "build a skill" and
# the other four notes about itself are delivered.
skills/eagent-development/
skills/eagent-create-plugin/
skills/eagent-debug-plugin/
skills/eagent-manage-plugin/
skills/eagent-plugin-router/
skills/eagent-review-plugin/
knowledge/main/about/architecture.md


###############################################################################
# ─── LAST SECTION: universal junk / caches (MUST BE LAST) ───
#   Put these at the *bottom* so they override any ! re‑includes above
###############################################################################
# OS / editor junk
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Python caches / compiled artefacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd

# Environment files anywhere. `**/`: a pattern without it matches the root
# of the build context only.
**/*.env
